# Line-ending and byte-exactness rules.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true rewrites these files into LF on commit,
# which silently breaks the Windows launcher:
#   - cmd.exe needs CRLF in .cmd files (goto labels and blocks misparse on LF)
#   - dsh-keepup.ps1 must keep its UTF-8 BOM, because Windows PowerShell 5.1
#     reads a BOM-less script as ANSI/GBK and turns the Chinese text into
#     mojibake or a parse error
#
# "* text=auto eol=lf" keeps the repository itself LF-normalized while the
# explicit rules below protect the files that must not be touched.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact: store and check out unchanged, so the BOM survives.
dsh-keepup.ps1 -text

# cmd.exe requires CRLF; store LF in the repo, check out CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Windows PowerShell scripts: same reason, and they double as editors' targets.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Windows script hosts and shells.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.vbs  text eol=crlf

# Documentation and source: LF everywhere.
*.md       text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.js       text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.svg      text eol=lf
*.gitignore text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never diff, never convert.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
